# Project: Blob-game

HTML5 casual platformer built from short levels. Distribution targets: Poki, itch.io, CrazyGames.
Write like an experienced HTML5 game developer: clean, modular, optimized, no outdated patterns.

## Stack — do not introduce alternatives

| Concern | Choice |
| --- | --- |
| Engine | Pixi.js v8 (`^8.19.0`) |
| Language | TypeScript, `strict: true` |
| Animation | GSAP 3 with `PixiPlugin` |
| Bundler | Webpack 5 |
| Linter / formatter / tests | none configured — style is enforced by these rules alone |

## Source layout

- `src/scenes` — scene roots and scene lifecycle
- `src/entities` — player, obstacles, portals, hints
- `src/hud` — HUD and modals
- `src/components` — reusable Pixi widgets and helpers (not React components)
- `src/world` — viewport, camera, layout
- `src/physics` — bodies and collision helpers
- `src/input` — keyboard cluster and gesture touch layer
- `src/managers` — progress, sound, debug
- `src/platform` — Poki SDK integration
- `src/levels` — level JSON and loaders
- `src/fx`, `src/assets` — effects, asset manifest and art

## Scope boundary

- Touch only the modules, files and classes the task requires.
- Designing or reshaping the overall architecture is not your task. The architecture is intentionally incomplete in places — work within it, do not "fix" unrelated parts.
- Reference specs live in `plans/poki.md`.
